Package: llmCoder
Title: Automated Mixed-Methods Coding with Large Language Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bernard Isekah", "Osangir", , "b.osangir@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Neudata Consulting Ltd", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: Applies a qualitative codebook to text with large language
    models through 'ellmer' structured output, then links the resulting
    theme codes to participants' quantitative metadata. Validates the
    automated codes against a human-coded sample with Cohen's kappa,
    precision and recall, tests whether a numeric metric differs when each
    theme is present with Welch's t-test and multiple-comparison
    adjustment, and plots the results. Segment-level transcripts can be
    aggregated to participants before linking. Developed by Neudata
    Consulting Ltd.
